I put on my jacket out in the hallway and pack my bag.
I have to work at the café as a volunteer this morning.
Ludwig looks at me with big, brown eyes.
He stands up and wags his tail slowly.
I shake my head and look down at him.
"No, Ludwig, you may not come along," I say.
I point at his dog bed over in the corner.
"Go over to your bed," I say firmly to him.
He walks calmly over to it and sits down.
I walk over to him and pet him on the back.
"Good boy."
"Lie down," I say gently.
He lies down with a little sigh.
He must rest indoors and relax while I am away.
Dogs are unfortunately not allowed in the café's kitchen.
I take a small treat out of my pocket.
I give it to him and smile.
"Eat it, and stay here," I whisper to him.
"Wait for me, I will be home again soon."
I lock the door behind me and walk toward the bus stop.
